  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with Kcnc2 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6 or Kcnv2, which then participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, ultimately leading to Kcnc2 being involved in this process. This indicates a potential mechanism where Guanidine may modulate potassium channel activity, influencing Kcnc2 function. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the specific target of Guanidine (Kcna6 vs. Kcnv2) remains distinct. The overlapping role of delayed rectifier potassium channels in these interactions implies a broader regulatory role for Guanidine in potassium channel function, potentially affecting Kcnc2 in a general manner.",
